i=c?"- The texture will be repeated across large surfaces, so every map must wrap perfectly on all four edges.\n- Make the material tile cleanly in a 3x3 grid without visible seams, jumps, mirrored edges, or repetition artifacts.\n- Remove perspective distortion, shadows, highlights, reflections, camera noise, text, logos, borders, objects, and lighting gradients before making the repeat.\n- Equalize the BaseColor/albedo so repeated tiles do not reveal brighter or darker stripes, bands, patches, stains, or other recognizable large-scale marks.\n":"- The texture will be stretched once over the assigned surface, not repeated as a tile.\n- Do not force the edges to match and do not create artificial mirrored, offset, cloned, or blended wrap seams.\n- Preserve the source as one coherent surface panel while removing perspective distortion, shadows, highlights, reflections, camera noise, text, logos, foreign objects, and unwanted lighting gradients.\n- Equalize the BaseColor/albedo so the single texture has an even material tone without broad brighter or darker stripes, bands, patches, stains, or lighting falloff.\n"
h=c?"Create a perfectly seamless square texture from the attached image.":"Create one coherent square single-texture image from the attached image."
g=c?"The texture must tile cleanly in a 3x3 grid without visible seams or repetition artifacts.":"The texture must be usable as one stretched image over the whole target surface and must not rely on tiled repetition."
f=c?"seamless baked BaseColor / preview texture":"single-use baked BaseColor / preview texture"
